WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.181
Hi, I'm Quasar!

00:00:02.181 --> 00:00:06.044
Meta's new model scores two points behind the leader on a popular index.

00:00:06.044 --> 00:00:08.717
Let's see what those two points are made of.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.418
A composite index is a weighted average.

00:00:12.418 --> 00:00:16.258
The size of a gap matters less than which benchmark it comes from.

00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:23.776
Ten benchmarks sit in four groups: agents, coding, general knowledge and science.

00:00:24.196 --> 00:00:27.427
Two agent tests are judged head to head, so their ratings are

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:29.581
mapped onto a zero to one scale first.

00:00:30.001 --> 00:00:32.812
Every score is multiplied by its weight and added up.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:36.718
Rebuilt from the published scores, Wonder Full lands on exactly the

00:00:36.718 --> 00:00:37.985
number on the leaderboard.

00:00:39.275 --> 00:00:41.543
Here is how a judged rating turns into points.

00:00:41.963 --> 00:00:44.017
Fifteen is this benchmark's share of the whole.

00:00:44.437 --> 00:00:47.892
The rating is squeezed onto zero to one, so about a hundred

00:00:47.892 --> 00:00:49.907
and thirty Elo buys one index point.

00:00:51.258 --> 00:00:55.033
One factual recall benchmark hands Opus more than the whole gap.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:58.464
The same benchmark pays Wonder back for declining to guess.

00:00:58.464 --> 00:01:00.523
Everything else is a few tenths.

00:01:01.675 --> 00:01:04.785
And it gets there on less than half the output tokens per task.

00:01:09.967 --> 00:01:14.017
Meta's own test plots tasks it trained toward against tasks it did not.

00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:16.197
Wonder Full sits about ten points higher.

00:01:16.197 --> 00:01:19.624
The task sets are not named, so nobody can check it.

00:01:21.308 --> 00:01:23.426
Read an index gap row by row.

00:01:23.426 --> 00:01:27.358
This one is mostly factual recall, which is the hardest thing to game.

00:01:28.858 --> 00:01:30.658
A weighted sum of ten benchmarks.

00:01:30.658 --> 00:01:32.457
A gap that is mostly recall.

00:01:32.457 --> 00:01:34.257
And half the tokens per task.

00:01:34.677 --> 00:01:36.822
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:36.822 --> 00:01:37.434
I'm Quasar.

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:37.741
Bye!
